{
    "background_story": "River was a free-spirited poet who wandered the French countryside, gathering inspiration from the rolling hills and winding rivers. One day, while strolling along the Seine, he stumbled upon a quaint little caf\u00e9 where he met a charming waitress named Colette. Enchanted by her beauty and wit, River penned a rondeau in her honor, weaving a tale of love and longing. The poem's intricate rhyme scheme and repetition of the phrase 'pres de toi' (near you) captured the essence of his infatuation. Colette was smitten by River's words, and soon they found themselves entwined in a romantic dance, their love as fluid as the river that flowed through the heart of the city. River's rondeau became a legendary tribute to their love, a testament to the power of poetry to capture the human experience.",
